      <workList xml:id="workDesc_4ffba713">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e234231">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_ecd9d608">B2:018</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="de">Cantata auf das heilige Oster-Fest</title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_b3476390" xml:lang="de">Mitten unter den Gedanken</title>
            <title type="subordinate" xml:id="title_5ffd01a0" xml:lang="de">In Festo Paschatos. Feria III</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_60cfbfdc">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_22_0">
               <eventList type="performances" xml:id="eventList_be945289">
                  <event xml:id="event_e05b37f3">
                     <date isodate="1770" xml:id="date_ccdcd0f1">Easter 1770</date>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_8e2f8f02">Zurich</geogName>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_3f601b7a">
                        <head xml:id="head_b84839a0">Reviews</head>
                        <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_1dcf4f0a">
                           <genre xml:id="genre_d6eadc96">article</genre>
                           <genre xml:id="genre_b837b678">journal</genre>
                           <title level="a" xml:id="title_aabf73a0"/>
                           <title level="j" xml:id="title_cb92ea73"/>
                        </bibl>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_c014922d">
                        <head xml:id="head_4158cf98">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm128">The present cantata of which only the printed text seems to have survived was composed before 1761 when it was listed in the Breitkopf catalogue of house manuscripts. This suggests that it was originally performed in Neukirche by Carl Gotthelf Gerlach; Breitkopf later acquired the work from the Gerlach estate in 1761. It was presumably from this catalogue that the work was ordered and then performed by the musical society or one of the churches in Zurich in 1770. The present cantata might have been performed on the same occasion as 'Der Herr wird zu uns kommen' (SchW B2:017 with which the present work is bound), since it clearly has been issued together with this work (continuous page numbers and no title page to the second cantata of the printed text). The libretto is interesting as it reveals details regarding the instrumentation of the various sections and includes also the chorale melodies to be sung by the choir and perhaps also by the audience or congregation.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_761c23e2">
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
               <language xml:id="de">German</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_29f007f8-fb91-4af9-85ba-f0091b34e9e7278">
